    "summary_one_sentence": "Set during World War II, self-exiled gangster Tommy Shelby must return to a blitzed Birmingham to stop a Nazi counterfeit currency plot involving his estranged son, Duke, and save his family's legacy.",
    "summary_short": "During the Birmingham Blitz in 1940, former mob boss Tommy Shelby lives in self-imposed exile, wracked by guilt and writing his memoirs. When his estranged son Duke assumes leadership of the Peaky Blinders and gets entangled with a Nazi operative in a plot to flood Britain with counterfeit money, Tommy is forced back into action. Following the tragic murder of his sister Ada, Tommy re-emerges to reclaim control of his gang and thwart the enemy scheme. Ultimately, Tommy faces a devastating personal reckoning to protect his family and preserve his nation.",
    "summary_long": "In November 1940, amidst the devastation of the Birmingham Blitz, Nazi agent John Beckett executes a clandestine operation to collapse the British economy using counterfeit currency. Reclusive former gang leader Tommy Shelby is living in isolation, haunted by visions of his past and the loss of his loved ones. Meanwhile, Tommy’s estranged son Duke leads a rogue faction of the Peaky Blinders, looting bombed sites and falling under Beckett's manipulation. When Tommy’s sister Ada discovers Duke’s involvement and attempts to alert authorities, Beckett murders her to preserve the operation. Grief-stricken and driven by duty to family and nation, Tommy returns to Birmingham, reassumes leadership of the Peaky Blinders, and plans a decisive counterstrike. Leveraging loyal allies across the city, Tommy traps Beckett’s mercenaries in an explosive ambush on the Liverpool docks and incinerates the fake banknotes. Though victorious in suppressing the Nazi plot and redeeming Duke, Tommy is mortally wounded during the final clash. Accepting his fate, Tommy finds peace at last as the next generation steps forward to carry the family legacy.",
    "synopsis": "Set against the dark backdrop of World War II during the peak of the Birmingham Blitz, Peaky Blinders: The Immortal Man continues the saga of the legendary Shelby crime family. After retreating into self-imposed exile and attempting to leave his violent past behind, iconic gangster Tommy Shelby is drawn back into the fray when Nazi operatives attempt to destabilize Great Britain through an insidious covert plot. With his estranged son Duke at risk of falling under enemy influence and the nation's security hanging in the balance, Tommy must navigate treacherous political webs, personal guilt, and old enemies to defend his family and protect his home.",
